00:27:34.050 --> 00:27:37.050
I'm going to an urgent meeting. See you tomorrow, at the newspaper!

00:27:37.050 --> 00:27:41.860
So what? What an asshole!

00:27:41.860 --> 00:27:49.910
Don't go! And don't come back!

00:27:49.910 --> 00:27:54.490
Go home! And have a good tisane!

00:27:54.490 --> 00:28:00.000
I'm starting to get tired of all these people who hallucinate, even in my own day!

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:03.330
A strange guy? You too have seen The Saviour?

00:28:03.330 --> 00:28:05.310
What is this stupid article?

00:28:05.310 --> 00:28:12.990
You think it's funny with your grotesque story of superheroes?

00:28:12.990 --> 00:28:16.090
You dreamed!

00:28:16.090 --> 00:28:18.090
And don't forget that I pay you to write sports pages

00:28:18.090 --> 00:28:22.100
and not paper novels!

00:28:22.100 --> 00:28:24.100
I saw it!

00:28:30.060 --> 00:28:33.720
- It exists! - Doctor, what a good arm you have!

00:28:33.720 --> 00:28:41.880
In truth, Mr. Commissioner, I would have liked to know about the sequels of the investigation

00:28:41.880 --> 00:28:45.600
on the murders and the disappearances in the region.

00:28:45.600 --> 00:28:49.000
The investigation is sadly flawed, I do not hide it.

00:28:49.000 --> 00:28:56.090
All we know is that these are two different cases.

00:28:56.090 --> 00:29:00.000
The bodies found present all traces of murder.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:05.120
It concerns young women from 16 to 25 years old.

00:29:05.120 --> 00:29:06.680
Extraordinary.

00:29:06.680 --> 00:29:13.090
For a few weeks, I've been observing in my office cases of acute schizophrenia.

00:29:13.090 --> 00:29:18.340
Young women with extreme violent crises.

00:29:18.340 --> 00:29:20.800
They feel like they're being abused.

00:29:20.800 --> 00:29:22.800
And you think that these crises could lead them to murder?

00:29:22.800 --> 00:29:25.000
I'm convinced.

00:29:25.000 --> 00:29:27.140
They seem to be manipulated.

00:29:47.080 --> 00:30:00.000
I heard about a mysterious creature who would make us competitors in the region by strangling poor natives.

00:30:00.320 --> 00:30:04.840
It reminds me of a Nostradamus prophecy

00:30:04.840 --> 00:30:07.880
that says something like this:

00:30:07.880 --> 00:30:15.270
"Two demons from a distant planet called "Assassina"

00:30:15.270 --> 00:30:21.250
will one day come to Earth to annihilate the human race.

00:30:21.250 --> 00:30:25.250
The "Assassina" planet.

00:30:25.250 --> 00:30:29.090
The exterminating demons.

00:30:31.080 --> 00:30:35.080
I will examine these creatures a lot.

00:30:35.080 --> 00:30:40.660
In the meantime, bring me other young women.

00:30:40.660 --> 00:30:44.630
I need to get my hands dirty.

00:30:44.630 --> 00:30:51.860
There have never been as many crimes in this city as these last few weeks.

00:30:51.860 --> 00:30:54.420
A little tour of the city is required.

00:31:04.700 --> 00:31:05.700
I'm sorry to bother you.

00:31:05.700 --> 00:31:07.980
No, no, I beg you, sit down.

00:31:07.980 --> 00:31:13.190
I'll have some coca again.

00:31:13.190 --> 00:31:14.050
Here.

00:31:14.050 --> 00:31:24.360
Ah, these mosquitoes are so annoying.

00:31:24.360 --> 00:31:27.600
Oh, last night I got completely devoured.

00:31:27.600 --> 00:31:29.560
But it's not surprising with these shells.

00:31:30.320 --> 00:31:33.520
I don't know anything more awful than mosquitoes.

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:02.000
this isolated countryside.

00:32:02.000 --> 00:32:04.010
I wonder if these cockroaches are inhabited.

00:32:04.010 --> 00:32:06.010
It would surprise me, it's desert.

00:32:06.010 --> 00:32:13.450
Do you know what we see in your region?

00:32:13.450 --> 00:32:17.140
It's not dirty, there are beautiful guys.

00:32:17.140 --> 00:32:19.950
I'm disappointed, on this side,

00:32:19.950 --> 00:32:22.600
I think it's not terrible. There are beautiful cows there.

00:32:22.600 --> 00:32:25.840
I speak seriously,

00:32:25.840 --> 00:32:27.920
they say that at night,

00:32:27.920 --> 00:32:30.000
horned monsters come out of the earth to capture

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:37.190
the pretty girls like us you think I'm going to walk you do as you want but it's true I read

00:32:37.190 --> 00:32:41.450
articles about it there are plenty of girls who have disappeared these days and we have never found

00:32:41.450 --> 00:33:00.000
their corpse you are stupid what you are fooling me I would not like to meet a monster

00:33:00.960 --> 00:33:03.260
Well, other monsters than you.

00:33:03.260 --> 00:33:04.540
You're really not funny.

00:33:04.540 --> 00:33:05.320
Hop, we break.

00:33:05.320 --> 00:33:06.200
That's it!

00:33:06.200 --> 00:33:09.750
Go throw yourself in their arms, they'll enjoy it.

00:33:09.750 --> 00:33:17.390
You're not one of them.

00:33:17.390 --> 00:33:19.730
It must be the girls next door.

00:33:19.730 --> 00:33:21.250
I'll go see.

00:33:21.250 --> 00:33:23.270
Be careful.

00:33:42.890 --> 00:33:44.440
It won't be good tonight.

00:34:01.180 --> 00:34:02.380
Are they our buddies?

00:34:02.380 --> 00:34:03.470
Oh, that's surprising.

00:34:55.790 --> 00:34:58.130
What do you have, miss?

00:34:58.130 --> 00:35:00.000
Well, there are two different gangs

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:06.540
in the region. One strangles its victims, leaving traces of burns, and the other only kidnaps very young women.

00:35:06.540 --> 00:35:11.170
- Like in Camping? - But those who attacked me really looked like prisoners.

00:35:11.170 --> 00:35:17.170
- Some even testify that several of the missing young women were seen again, and manifested signs of inactivity.

00:35:17.170 --> 00:35:30.000
- Hello, this is the News of the West. - Dr. Killerman was not dead.

00:35:33.930 --> 00:35:34.930
What did you see?

00:35:34.930 --> 00:35:37.260
We were having dinner under the tent.

00:35:37.260 --> 00:35:38.150
There were mosquitoes.

00:35:38.150 --> 00:35:40.260
Suddenly, we heard noise.

00:35:40.260 --> 00:35:44.150
We went out and then we saw people fighting in the next tent.

00:35:44.150 --> 00:35:46.120
Can you describe these people to me?

00:35:46.120 --> 00:35:47.120
We saw them badly, it was night.

00:35:47.120 --> 00:35:50.120
I went out a little later and saw two people running away.

00:35:50.120 --> 00:35:53.200
I saw a lot more, six or seven at least.

00:35:53.200 --> 00:35:55.200
So, how many were they exactly?

00:35:55.200 --> 00:35:56.250
They were two.

00:35:56.250 --> 00:35:58.200
They moved away in silence.

00:35:58.200 --> 00:36:00.000
You said there were people?

00:36:00.030 --> 00:36:02.890
It wasn't them who were screaming. They were very calm.

00:36:02.890 --> 00:36:05.840
And anyway, they had big leather masks, like mausoleums.

00:36:05.840 --> 00:36:09.870
Not at all. They were dressed like soldiers, with turtlenecks.

00:36:09.870 --> 00:36:13.950
No, you saw badly. They were hiding under their clothes, Mr. Commissioner.

00:36:13.950 --> 00:36:17.980
Oh, so that. You too were afraid. You were trembling like a dead bird.

00:36:17.980 --> 00:36:21.330
Miss, you know what a false testimony is worth.

00:36:21.330 --> 00:36:23.480
Now, it will be necessary to agree.

00:36:23.480 --> 00:36:29.540
Either it was the Great Badrouille, or it was the meeting of the Rossetti.

00:36:30.510 --> 00:36:31.570
I'm going to do it again

00:37:41.440 --> 00:37:43.440
Too bad, Boris!

00:37:43.440 --> 00:37:50.570
The K-Gland is stuck between the hypothalamus and the retrohormones!

00:37:50.570 --> 00:37:54.900
We'll see about that with the other girl!

00:38:00.960 --> 00:38:07.910
"Install the new specimen! We'll see how it reacts!"

00:38:37.130 --> 00:38:43.600
The reactivation serum, Boris.

00:38:43.600 --> 00:38:48.630
As for me, I will proceed to the trepanation.

00:39:16.190 --> 00:39:19.300
The glanca is over-activated!

00:39:30.860 --> 00:39:32.180
There's already less wind here.

00:39:32.180 --> 00:39:36.850
Yes, I really can't take it anymore.

00:39:36.850 --> 00:39:38.040
How's your knee?

00:39:38.040 --> 00:39:41.600
Yeah, it's fine.

00:39:41.600 --> 00:39:51.670
We have a visitor.

00:39:51.670 --> 00:39:53.970
Are they boys?

00:40:03.840 --> 00:40:22.640
You must be a hunter!

00:40:22.640 --> 00:40:25.320
But I hope you noticed that there is no "you" in your refuge!

00:40:25.320 --> 00:40:28.930
Well, we're not going to die again!

00:40:28.930 --> 00:40:30.000
Tiens!

00:40:44.010 --> 00:40:45.110
You're alive !

00:40:45.110 --> 00:40:46.480
Watch out, they're escaping !

00:41:00.250 --> 00:41:07.220
It's you, the special sender of news from the West!

00:41:07.220 --> 00:41:15.010
Welcome to my little press conference!

00:41:15.010 --> 00:41:22.210
I'm going to talk to you about me and then I'll let you go.

00:42:02.970 --> 00:42:11.490
You see, my Cartesian spirit is completed by this artistic temperament.

00:42:11.490 --> 00:42:26.180
Art brings me a great balance, but deep down, scientific research is not joined by the search for beauty.

00:42:33.840 --> 00:42:34.740
No, you!

00:43:19.130 --> 00:43:21.940
to the young girl during the last rave.

00:43:21.940 --> 00:43:24.230
It's annoying.

00:43:24.230 --> 00:43:27.910
Her operation didn't work.

00:43:27.910 --> 00:43:30.000
But I know why.

00:43:30.280 --> 00:43:38.020
I will have to reinforce the over-activation of the Gland K for our next patients.

00:43:38.020 --> 00:43:42.710
But let's see the specimen that you brought us.

00:43:42.710 --> 00:43:52.560
Maurice must have thought about drugging her.

00:44:00.000 --> 00:44:03.930
You are a beautiful specimen, miss!

00:44:03.930 --> 00:44:06.400
I congratulate you!

00:44:06.400 --> 00:44:12.170
And if I could, I would also congratulate your parents!

00:44:12.170 --> 00:44:17.220
Come on Boris, let's prepare our revenge!

00:45:42.670 --> 00:45:46.950
the stars? Yes, once, and I caught the flu.

00:45:46.950 --> 00:45:54.130
Is that true? No, I'm kidding. It happens to me sometimes too. I'm sure

00:45:54.130 --> 00:46:00.000
that there are other planets inhabited in the universe. But tell me, do you hope you

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:04.000
to see the savior with his big red cape flying over the houses.

00:46:04.000 --> 00:46:05.250
Don't make fun of me.

00:46:05.250 --> 00:46:08.130
If you knew how I would like to meet him again,

00:46:08.130 --> 00:46:10.050
it would be the most beautiful moment of my life.

00:46:10.050 --> 00:46:11.810
It may be possible.

00:46:11.810 --> 00:46:12.840
Do you know him?

00:46:12.840 --> 00:46:15.520
I had the opportunity to meet him too.

00:46:15.520 --> 00:46:20.400
He's a charming man, even if he's a little special.

00:46:20.400 --> 00:46:23.680
And you could get me an interview with him?

00:46:23.680 --> 00:46:26.760
I'll try.

00:46:26.760 --> 00:46:29.760
Either tomorrow at midnight,

00:46:30.000 --> 00:46:39.690
Let's talk a little bit. How are you feeling now?

00:46:39.690 --> 00:46:45.590
I want to pee. What is your new goal in life?

00:46:45.590 --> 00:46:50.830
Wash socks? Do the kitchen?

00:46:50.830 --> 00:46:57.970
Or dye your nails in green? I want to obey Dr. Keeley.

00:46:57.970 --> 00:47:00.000
Dr. Keeley is my best friend.

00:47:01.310 --> 00:47:06.530
This young woman will be the best element of my army!

00:47:06.530 --> 00:47:13.810
And I could rule the world with terror and crime!

00:47:13.810 --> 00:47:18.950
I feel like I'm going to have a good time!

00:48:38.540 --> 00:48:50.580
Miss, you are safe here. I prescribed you calms.

00:48:50.580 --> 00:48:53.980
I would like to know what you have lived, it's important.

00:48:53.980 --> 00:48:57.370
Try to remember.

00:48:57.370 --> 00:49:00.000
I do not remember anything.

00:49:01.340 --> 00:49:03.170
I don't know.

00:49:03.170 --> 00:49:10.920
When you were found, you were alone on a railway track.

00:49:10.920 --> 00:49:16.910
And you were wearing this.

00:49:16.910 --> 00:49:18.870
I don't remember.

00:49:18.870 --> 00:49:20.140
Try again.

00:49:20.140 --> 00:49:21.860
It's important.

00:49:21.860 --> 00:49:24.600
Where did you come from?

00:49:24.600 --> 00:49:28.390
Who were you with?

00:49:28.390 --> 00:49:30.000
What were you doing?

00:49:52.140 --> 00:49:55.090
The surgery, the doctor, it was awful!

00:49:55.090 --> 00:49:58.610
Draw! Draw what comes to mind!

00:50:16.700 --> 00:50:24.960
What a mess, you say?

00:50:42.090 --> 00:50:55.670
You who are an ass and a fine pister, bring me these creatures so nice, they will be of great use!

00:51:00.410 --> 00:51:00.930
I don't know.

00:53:16.000 --> 00:53:18.280
It's your savior's story again, who's shooting you in the head!

00:53:18.280 --> 00:53:19.520
This time, I've got photos!

00:53:19.520 --> 00:53:20.160
Let me see.

00:53:32.590 --> 00:53:35.570
I never had time to work. Look at all these names.

00:53:35.570 --> 00:53:38.040
How do you want me to put this in my column?

00:53:38.040 --> 00:53:42.490
Everyone dies in this region, we are in synchro mode.

00:53:42.490 --> 00:53:47.030
So, would the savior really exist?

00:53:47.030 --> 00:53:50.710
I don't understand anything about what's going on in these islands.

00:53:50.710 --> 00:53:54.550
But you have to have the exclusivity of all this.

00:54:11.450 --> 00:54:14.950
Creatures have been spotted in this area, let's be careful.

00:54:45.580 --> 00:54:48.600
The frogs don't sing anymore.

00:54:48.600 --> 00:54:53.860
The creature we're looking for has gone this way.

00:54:53.860 --> 00:54:55.550
Look!

00:54:55.550 --> 00:54:58.570
Traces of the ground.

00:54:58.570 --> 00:54:59.410
It's naked.

00:55:19.360 --> 00:55:22.660
I feel you, you're almost there.

00:55:53.680 --> 00:55:55.500
- They took him! - It's too dangerous!

00:55:55.500 --> 00:55:58.010
- The doctor sends us to death! - Yes, but we're well paid!

00:55:58.010 --> 00:56:00.000
- And it's suicide! - Yes, but it's a paid suicide!

00:56:47.440 --> 00:56:49.190
of the world.

00:56:49.190 --> 00:56:52.090
I'm crazy!

00:56:52.090 --> 00:56:55.350
She's going to pay for it!

00:56:55.350 --> 00:56:58.870
They're all going to pay for it!

00:57:00.000 --> 00:57:05.950
My name is Isabelle, I am 21 years old, I play volleyball, I like to read and draw.

00:57:05.950 --> 00:57:11.520
It is an honour for me to represent the Nouvelles de l'Ouest at the Miss Press Local 1993 competition.

00:57:35.150 --> 00:57:36.690
Your boss seems to be excited.

00:57:36.690 --> 00:57:37.750
Better for him.

00:57:37.750 --> 00:57:40.340
Me, this kind of beauty contest annoys me.

00:57:40.340 --> 00:57:42.210
Still going for the camisoles.

00:57:42.210 --> 00:57:46.960
My name is Grazia, I'm 22 years old, I love the dress and the equipment.

00:58:11.710 --> 00:58:29.670
And here is our last candidate

00:58:30.000 --> 00:58:33.990
With that, we can only succeed at the local press conference in 1993.

00:58:33.990 --> 00:58:36.870
But I will not monopolize the speech any longer.

00:58:36.870 --> 00:58:40.560
Because I know you came to see the candidates, but also to drink.

00:58:40.560 --> 00:58:42.700
The buffet is open.

00:58:42.700 --> 00:58:44.700
Error! It just came to close!

00:58:44.700 --> 00:58:59.120
Ladies and gentlemen, do not panic!

00:58:59.120 --> 00:59:00.000
Do what you have to do!

00:59:01.850 --> 00:59:26.460
Some of you may already know me through a very, very bad article that "Votre Feuille de Chou" has published recently.

00:59:26.460 --> 00:59:30.000
But what do you want?

00:59:30.480 --> 00:59:35.480
Sorry my little intrusion in your so charming meeting.

00:59:35.480 --> 00:59:44.210
But I've always been like that, as soon as I see light somewhere, it makes me want to enter.

01:00:11.840 --> 01:00:12.840
Maudira.

01:00:12.840 --> 01:00:26.820
But it is this mean young girl who has put a very bad foot on Dr. Kill.

01:00:32.330 --> 01:00:36.050
- What can we do? - First of all, we can avoid falling into the hands of these brutes.

01:00:36.050 --> 01:00:40.160
- He didn't read my paper. - Yeah, I have the impression that he didn't.

01:00:40.160 --> 01:00:52.340
- The presentation has already started, I'm a little late. - Stay here.

01:00:52.340 --> 01:00:57.490
- I'm going to try to get some help. - Oh, if only the Savior could come to our aid.

01:00:57.490 --> 01:00:59.090
Do you think he could pull us out of here?

01:01:00.190 --> 01:01:02.440
I don't know.

01:01:34.760 --> 01:01:37.950
Hello? Is that you, Clermont?

01:01:37.950 --> 01:01:41.250
This is the Saviour!

01:01:41.250 --> 01:01:44.730
Oh, but he's an old friend!

01:01:44.730 --> 01:01:47.600
Bring me back this useless superhero!

01:02:32.360 --> 01:02:37.220
But I don't like to play with my toys for too long, you know that, Boris!

01:02:37.220 --> 01:02:43.030
Come on! Let's finish this with the Savior!

01:03:14.200 --> 01:03:17.840
In fact, we can no longer put our hands on the Savior, Dr. Keel.

01:03:17.840 --> 01:03:26.970
But I see that the Savior is like me, he loves to play with little soldiers!

01:03:26.970 --> 01:03:29.090
Mr. Nathan!

01:03:33.070 --> 01:03:35.070
Ok, I'm ready! Go!

01:04:08.920 --> 01:04:15.730
Leave it there, you'll see.

01:04:15.730 --> 01:04:21.250
You won't have Elina, but I will have you.

01:04:41.420 --> 01:04:43.420
I took care of your orders.

01:04:45.750 --> 01:04:49.910
It would be wise, I think, to regain our laboratory.

01:04:51.760 --> 01:04:53.910
With its specimens.

01:05:20.540 --> 01:05:22.760
There is no limit to what you can do.

01:05:39.080 --> 01:05:42.360
Ah! My good old reporter outfit!

01:05:42.360 --> 01:05:44.090
It's been a long time.

01:05:44.090 --> 01:05:46.480
Nothing happened in this fucking city.

01:05:46.480 --> 01:05:49.880
Give me the scoop!

01:05:49.880 --> 01:05:53.990
Give me the glory!

01:06:58.030 --> 01:07:00.000
With a scoop like that, watch your mouth.

01:07:00.670 --> 01:07:02.310
It's arranged at the Arbrique des Fêtes d'hiver

01:08:42.060 --> 01:08:51.060
I know the admirable editor-in-chief of the famous newspaper "Les Nouvelles Ouest"!

01:08:51.060 --> 01:08:57.180
Listen, it's a misunderstanding. I was passing by by chance. I was picking mushrooms.

01:08:57.180 --> 01:09:00.000
But what were you doing?

01:09:00.030 --> 01:09:06.230
to collect mushrooms in these pestilent swamps in the sky!

01:09:06.230 --> 01:09:07.430
But what do you want?

01:09:07.430 --> 01:09:12.520
I would just like some information, my good sir.

01:09:12.520 --> 01:09:17.630
What exactly do you know about the Savior,

01:09:17.630 --> 01:09:22.090
this grotesque superhero that annoys me so much?

01:09:22.090 --> 01:09:23.170
I don't know anything.

01:09:23.170 --> 01:09:28.140
Think about what I can bring you.

01:09:28.140 --> 01:09:30.000
I became a master in...

01:09:31.050 --> 01:09:34.960
Manipulate the psychism of young women.

01:09:34.960 --> 01:09:41.100
Isn't there, by the way, in your editorial a certain Helena?

01:09:41.100 --> 01:09:47.100
Well, think that with a simple little bite of bistouri,

01:09:47.100 --> 01:09:52.010
I could make her madly in love with you.

01:09:52.010 --> 01:09:54.190
You could really do that.

01:09:54.190 --> 01:09:58.070
Where is the saver?

01:09:58.070 --> 01:10:00.000
It works.

01:10:00.030 --> 01:10:04.280
He's a few steps away from here. He'll be here in a minute or two.

01:10:04.280 --> 01:10:12.600
You're so nice!

01:10:12.600 --> 01:10:28.380
Come on, we don't have much time left to prepare a little reception in honor of our friend, the saviour!

01:10:28.380 --> 01:10:30.000
*music*

01:10:30.190 --> 01:10:32.720
Hey gentlemen, I'm waiting for you!

01:10:32.720 --> 01:10:41.620
Bring us this miserableness!

01:10:41.620 --> 01:10:49.210
I have never been able to stand the cockroaches on the ceiling!

01:10:53.980 --> 01:10:56.280
Doctor who wants it, alive!

01:10:56.280 --> 01:10:58.070
Do you think it's easy?

01:11:07.710 --> 01:11:09.710
Tom would be invincible...

01:11:33.710 --> 01:11:41.760
Dr. Keel, where are you?

01:11:41.760 --> 01:11:47.360
Hello, dear savers!

